test_arpretx — ARP-driven TCP retransmit self-test
====================================================

Phase 1 chunk 2 of the net-stack quality plan: when
`inet_tcp_emit` hits an ARP miss for a non-loopback peer it now
sets `tcp_sockets[s].arp_pending = 1`.  When the matching ARP
reply later lands, `inet_arp_drain_pending` walks TCP, clears
the flag, and force-retransmits via `inet_tcp_retransmit`.
Saves a full RTO on the first SYN to any off-cache peer.

This test triggers the inet self-test that drives the state
machine synthetically — no real network, no real ARP.

Prints `arpretx: ok` on pass or `arpretx: failed N` where N is
the failure-step code returned by the inet self-test.

    module oskit.bin.test_arpretx

    import oskit.ulib.{puts, exit, exit_with}
    import oskit.net.{tcp_arp_replay_test}


    print_udec(v: int)
        if v >= 10
            print_udec(v / 10)
        var b: [1]byte
        b[0] = byte('0' + (v % 10))
        puts(string(&b[0], 1))


    fail(code: int)
        puts("arpretx: failed ")
        print_udec(code)
        puts("\n")
        exit_with(code)


    main(argv: []string)
        val rc = tcp_arp_replay_test()
        if rc != 0
            fail(rc)
            return
        puts("arpretx: ok\n")
        exit()
